    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> have a binomial distribution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;such that the sum and the product of the mean and variance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>128</mn></math>&nbsp;respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is equal to",
